{'symbol': 'PCAR', 'date': '2020-04-21 10:30:00', 'title': 'Paccar Achieves Good Quarterly Revenues And Profits', 'text': "PACCAR ACHIEVES GOOD QUARTERLY REVENUES AND PROFITS.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.03.Q1 REVENUE $5.16 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $4.9 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.21 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.PACCAR - Q1 TRUCK DELIVERIES WERE IMPACTED BY TEMPORARY CLOSURES OF CO'S TRUCK MANUFACTURING FACILITIES WORLDWIDE.PACCAR - Q1 INCLUDED HIGHER ACCRUALS FOR PRODUCT SUPPORT COSTS AND LOWER USED TRUCK RESULTS.MANUFACTURING CASH AND MARKETABLE SECURITIES WERE $4.3 BILLION AT MARCH 31, CO ALSO HAS ACCESS TO COMMITTED BANK FACILITIES OF $3.0 BILLION.REDUCED 2020 CAPEX BY $100 MILLION TO RANGE OF $525 MILLION -$575 MILLION, LOWERED RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT EXPENSES BY $45 MILLION TO RANGE OF $265 MILLION - $295 MILLION.OUTLOOK FOR GLOBAL ECONOMIES AND TRUCK MARKETS IS WEAKER DUE TO CORONAVIRUS PANDEMIC.DIFFICULT TO ESTIMATE 2020 TRUCK INDUSTRY RETAIL SALES IN NORTH AMERICA, EUROPE AND SOUTH AMERICA."}
{'symbol': 'PM', 'date': '2020-04-21 09:30:00', 'title': 'Philip Morris International Reports Qtrly Adjusted Diluted EPS Of $1.21', 'text': "QTRLY ADJUSTED DILUTED EPS OF $1.21, UP BY 11.0%; UP BY 30.1% ON A LIKE-FOR-LIKE BASIS, EXCLUDING CURRENCY.WITHDRAWS 2020 FULL-YEAR REPORTED DILUTED EPS FORECAST DUE SOLELY TO UNCERTAINTY RELATED TO COVID-19 PANDEMIC.BUSINESS CONTINUITY MEASURES ARE OPERATING EFFECTIVELY.EXPERIENCED A LIMITED IMPACT ON PERFORMANCE FROM THE EARLY STAGES OF THE COVID-19 PANDEMIC.PHILIP MORRIS - HAVE TO ASSUME THAT, IN SOME MARKETS, UNEMPLOYMENT, RELATED CUT IN DISPOSABLE INCOME WILL HAVE TEMPORARY IMPACT ON MARKET DYNAMICS.PHILIP MORRIS INTERNATIONAL - HAS A ROBUST FINANCIAL POSITION.PHILIP MORRIS INTERNATIONAL - LARGE MAJORITY OF CO'S MANUFACTURING FACILITIES GLOBALLY ARE OPERATIONAL, INCLUDING ALL HEATED TOBACCO UNIT FACTORIES.PHILIP MORRIS - CIGARETTE PRODUCTION FACILITIES TEMPORARILY IMPACTED BY SHUTDOWNS OR LIMITATIONS ACCOUNT FOR ABOUT 20% OF CO'S TOTAL CAPACITY.PHILIP MORRIS - BASED ON CURRENT SALES TRENDS, THERE ARE ADEQUATE INVENTORIES OF OVER TWO MONTHS FOR HEATED TOBACCO UNITS.PHILIP MORRIS - BASED ON CURRENT SALES TRENDS, THERE ARE ADEQUATE INVENTORIES OF OVER 3 MONTHS FOR TOBACCO HEATING DEVICES.PHILIP MORRIS - BASED ON CURRENT SALES TRENDS, THERE ARE ADEQUATE INVENTORIES OF OVER ONE AND A HALF MONTHS FOR CIGARETTES.PHILIP MORRIS INTERNATIONAL - DOES NOT CURRENTLY ANTICIPATE OUT-OF-STOCK SITUATIONS IN ANY MAJOR OPERATING INCOME MARKETS."}
